# Sovereign Infrastructure Architecture (SIA): Airport Behavioral Orchestration Framework

## Executive Summary
Traditional airport modernization frameworks focus heavily on perception and tracking—investing heavily in facial recognition, biometric kiosks, and complex passenger-tracking systems. Yet, major operational bottlenecks persist during peak seasons. 

The **SIA Airport Framework** shifts the paradigm from *perception* to *governance*. This repository outlines a solution architecture engineered to address the root cause of airport congestion: predictable and unpredictable human variables. By introducing data-decoupled tokenization and behavioral incentives, this framework shifts high-friction exceptions (e.g., non-compliant baggage or late arrivals) away from peak windows, preserving operational capacity and protecting legacy infrastructure from cascade failures.

